 "intro": "Quiberon Bay, off the coast of Brittany, 56 BC. The Veneti, a seafaring people, have risen against Caesar. You are Decimus Junius Brutus, commanding Caesar’s newly built galleys against about 220 tall sailing ships of oak.",
 "debrief": "In Caesar’s account, the Veneti ships were too high and strong for ramming. The Romans used sharp hooks on long poles to cut the halyards, bringing down the yards and leaving the ships helpless, then boarded them. Caesar and the army watched from the shore. When the wind dropped, the remaining Veneti ships were becalmed and taken one by one. Caesar executed the Veneti council and sold the people, because they had held Roman envoys. The other choices are what-ifs.",
